<title>INDIA: INDIA SEBI TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE TUESDAY.</title>
<headline>INDIA SEBI TO HOLD NEWS CONFERENCE TUESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's market regulator, the Securities &amp; Exchange Board of India (SEBI) said it will hold a news conference at 5.00 p.m. (1130 GMT) on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The capital market watchdog is expected to announce a decision on the proposed introduction of an easier carry-forward trading system, the SEBI spokesperson said.</p>
<p>A committee appointed by SEBI in July recommended an easier carry-forward system that will abolish twin-track system of segregating carry-forward trades and delivery trades, elimination of a limit of 90 days for transactions and a 100-million-rupee limit on funding.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91) 22-265 9000; Fax (91) 22-264 1699</p>
